 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\n\nProcessing Budget Billing Plans\n\nWhen periodic billing documents are invoiced, a new budget billing plan is created automatically for contracts that were billed\nperiodically. The budget billing plan is based on the budget billing extrapolation lines, which are generated by the billing document.\nA reference to the bill to be created is stored in the header of the budget billing plan in the Inv. doc. no. field (invoicing document\nnumber), so that information about future budget billings is shown on the bill. For information about other options for grouping\n\nbudget billings of the different contracts of a budget billing plan, see the documentation for the Budget Billing Plan (IS-U-IN-BB)\ncomponent.\n\nIf budget billing plans relate to the billed period of a billing document, then they are processed in invoicing on the basis of the\nbilling procedure used.\n\nInvoicing can consist of the following steps:\n\ne Deactivate budget billing plan\nThe invoicing document number appears automatically in the budget billing plan header in the Deactivate field.\nThis means that:\no You cannot further process the budget billing plan.\no All budget billing plan items are deactivated.\no The budget billing amounts cannot be paid, dunned or requested.\ne Deactivate budget billing plan items\n\nOpen items in the invoicing period are deactivated if the invoicing document number is set as the clearing document\nnumber.\n\n1   Note that the deactivated budget billing plan items:\n\no Cannot be further processed.\n\no Cannot be paid, dunned or requested.\n\ne Settle the budget billing payments (statistical budget billing plan procedure) or budget billing receivables against the\namount invoiced for the contract (partial billing procedure).\n\nOn the basis of the selected budget billing procedure, budget billing payments or receivables that have been made, are\ndeducted from the billing document. (See Customizing for |}}SAP Utilities } Invoicing \u00bb Basic Settings \u00bb Define System\n\nSettings for Invoicing 3).\n\no Budget billing payments which have been made and recorded as payments in contract accounts receivable and\npayable, can be reposted into the total in invoicing. This is part of the statistical budget billing plan procedure.\n\nAs aresult the budget billing and the new business partner item budget billing reposting are cleared by a new\naccounts receivable and payable document which is created in invoicing. The bill receivable of the invoicing\ndocument is cleared against the budget billing payments.\n\no The bill receivable is reduced in invoicing by the budget billing amounts, which are set as debits in the partial billing\nprocedure.\n",
